  "[prose] Mass also showed evidence of being under the influence of past selective pressures. Based solely on the levels of variation in mass present in the two castes, it would seem that mass was under stronger selection in workers than gynes, as gyne mass displayed significantly more variability than worker mass. However, this conclusion was not supported by gyne and worker intracaste phenotypic correlations.",
